      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The miscalculation of the p-value is more than a \"technicality\"; it directly undermines the primary evidence supporting the 95% claim, which is the objective of the research. While the compelling *trend* noted by the reviewers is valuable, a \"groundbreaking\" claim must be rigorously supported, and the current data cannot support it. This issue will likely demand a thorough and potentially complex statistical revision, possibly moving beyond a simple \"limitations\" mention to address the core validity of the results.",
